# Integer32 literal below the minimum

Verifies a negated int32 literal whose unsigned part exceeds the 32-bit
range is rejected with a compile-time diagnostic through the complete CLI
pipeline, consistent with int8 and int64.

>>> source
too_small: int32 = -2147483648
print(too_small)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `2147483648` for type `int32`: number too large to fit in target type at Span { start: 20, end: 30 }

<<< exit
1
